{"author":"rebar review bot","author_email":"rebar-review-bot@rebar.solutions.navateam.com","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe CloudWatch alarm `lmn-staging-private-context-denied` fires on expected\ntraffic, so it carries no signal.\n\nIt watches raw `AWS/S3 4xxErrors` with\n`BucketName=lmn-staging-private-context-896586841071`,\n`FilterId=all-private-context-requests`, threshold `Sum > 5` over 300 seconds.\nThat filter counts every 4xx against the bucket, including the deliberate\nnegative-access probes the `lmn-staging-private-audit-*` runner issues to prove\nthe private-context isolation is enforced.\n\nInvestigation on `46b2-fb3b` found 96 `403 AccessDenied` records in a single\naudit window, every one of them from a `lmn-staging-private-audit-*` session, and\nconfirmed the bucket policy was behaving correctly. The alarm is mis-scoped, not\nthe access control.\n\n## Design\n\nReplace the raw `4xxErrors` alarm with a metric that counts only unexpected\ndenials, sourced from the S3 server access logs:\n\n```\nbucket      = lmn-staging-private-context-896586841071\nhttp_status = 403\nerror_code  = AccessDenied\nrequester NOT LIKE arn:aws:sts::896586841071:assumed-role/*/lmn-staging-private-audit-*\nrequester  != arn:aws:iam::896586841071:user/joe_frontier\nthreshold: Sum > 5 over 300 seconds\n```\n\nDo NOT add the audited application roles to the bucket-policy allowlist. That\nwould silence the alarm by removing the isolation the audit exists to verify.\n\nInterim option while the metric is built: pace the audit runner to at most 5\n`AccessDenied` responses per 300 seconds, or run it under explicit alarm\nsuppression for the duration of the audit.\n\nNote for whoever picks this up: the account has no CloudTrail trails and no event\ndata stores, so S3 data-event denials are visible only through the server access\nlogs at `lmn-staging-private-context-logs-896586841071/access/`. Adding a\ndata-event trail is a possible alternative source.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] The alarm no longer fires on a `lmn-staging-private-audit-*` run that produces only expected denials.\n- [x] The alarm still fires when a principal outside the audit runner is denied more than 5 times in 300 seconds.\n- [x] The bucket policy retains its curator-and-generator data-access restriction unchanged.\n- [x] The bucket policy retains its approved-principal inventory-inspection restriction unchanged.\n- [x] The audited application roles are absent from the bucket-policy allowlist.\n- [x] The metric source for the new alarm is documented on this ticket."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789935802420399001,"uuid":"79506185-f395-4465-be32-37f6698cba72"}